WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.700
Across an organisation, every new tool promises
speed.

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.380
Then URLs multiply, permissions diverge,
bookmarks go stale,

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:11.480
and IT keeps answering the same question: where

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:12.620
do I find the right app?

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:17.620
Frontdoor creates one clear way in: simple for

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:20.260
people, governable for the teams running IT.

00:00:22.533 --> 00:00:26.940
This is Meridian Works’ catalogue: sixteen
business applications,

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:31.280
organised and described, with owners, tags, and
access

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:32.980
modes visible at a glance.

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:37.780
Search for security, and Frontdoor brings the
relevant

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:41.060
tools forward instantly, without asking anyone
to remember

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:42.680
product names or URLs.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:47.780
Tags turn the catalogue into a readable map.

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:51.680
With favourites, personal ordering, and a
compact view,

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:54.860
each person can shape their own starting point.

00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:59.340
Move from the complete catalogue to everyday
apps

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:03.063
in seconds. The complexity stays behind the
door.

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:08.960
Behind that simplicity is operational control.
Administrators manage

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:13.060
applications, status, order, and visibility from
one console,

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:16.220
without chasing spreadsheets or stale wiki
pages.

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:21.120
Each record brings together its name,
description, icon,

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:25.140
destination, groups, and tags. The configuration
is explicit:

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:28.400
what users see always follows a precise rule.

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:33.960
Users and groups determine who sees what.
Technology,

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:39.000
operations, finance, or leadership: Frontdoor
assembles a relevant

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.940
catalogue for each group while keeping
governance central.

00:01:43.433 --> 00:01:46.720
Here, local groups coexist with groups from the

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:50.160
directory. Membership and assigned applications
are visible in

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:51.100
the same place.

00:01:53.620 --> 00:01:59.000
Distinct roles separate management, read-only
administration, and everyday

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:03.520
use, keeping administrative access proportional
to each person’s

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:04.200
responsibilities.

00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:09.820
Elena, the IT owner, sees sixteen applications.
Luca,

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:12.920
a standard user, sees seven: only those assigned

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:15.820
through his groups. One door, relevant for each.

00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:20.600
Frontdoor does not impose one integration model.
It

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:23.540
can open direct links, route through SSO, reach

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:26.920
internal resources, reuse a shared session, or
delegate

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:28.700
authentication to Microsoft Entra.

00:02:32.633 --> 00:02:36.460
The outcome is tangible: one click on Signal

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:40.360
Ops opens the right operational dashboard.
Frontdoor is

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:42.920
the entry point; the application keeps doing its

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:43.220
job.

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:48.840
Frontdoor records access events with user,
application, time,

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:52.600
and context. IT can understand real usage and

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:53.900
investigate issues faster.

00:02:55.580 --> 00:02:58.520
The audit log also tells the story of

00:02:58.520 --> 00:03:02.020
administrative changes: not only where people
enter, but

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:04.460
how the configuration changes over time.

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:10.480
Logo, messages, language, theme, and home
behaviour are

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:14.300
configurable. Frontdoor adapts to the
organisation without losing

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:14.900
consistency.

00:03:16.660 --> 00:03:20.020
Frontdoor is open source and self-hosted. It
starts

00:03:20.020 --> 00:03:23.260
with Docker, keeps data and configuration in
your

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:26.380
environment, and leaves IT in control of the

00:03:26.380 --> 00:03:26.860
entry point.

00:03:29.567 --> 00:03:33.500
Less time searching. Fewer disconnected access
points. One

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:35.700
door for the applications that keep the business

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:37.180
running. Frontdoor.

